{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested","id":1400898,"title":"Armour Evocations: Feedback Requested","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-03T21:15:10-07:00","id":1400898,"title":"Armour Evocations: Feedback Requested","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Forged during the Shogunate, Ebony Fronds was first forged from steel and green jade, heated over ancient willow charcoal, then tempered with vegetable oil and soap and the sap of certain Eastern thistles for the Eastern Outcaste Busujima Clan\u2019s eldest son, Shutaro, who wore it in many battles and in time of peace, set it where rain and sun could reach it. In due course, it passed into the hands of other sons, and less often daughters, of the Clan. As with their other great treasures, the Clan took great pride in knowing that they had never had to ransom it back from their enemies. After the clan\u2019s destruction, it passed into the hands of Saeko Takagi, their former retainer and recently Exalted Dawn Caste.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Created for a man noted for his fastidious nature, the armour keeps itself and its attuned wearer clean, as per the Collar of Dawn\u2019s Cleansing Light. Given the great difficulty of keeping lamellar armour clean and pest-free with its intricate lacings, this is a considerable benefit. It also incorporates a hearthstone socket, which currently holds the keep\u2019s Monkey Stone.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Evocations of Ebony Fronds</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Leaf-Whisper Imitation</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Resonant</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Instant</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: None</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Ebony Fronds\u2019 overlapping scales become as silent and soft as leaves. This Evocation enhances a Stealth roll made while in plant-based concealment, lowering any penalties by the wearer\u2019s (Essence).</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Special activation rules</b>: As long as the wearer isn\u2019t dissonant with jade, this Evocation awakens at no cost when she successfully ambushes a non-trivial enemy.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Resonant</b>: As long as the wearer\u2019s roll beats at least one non-trivial enemy, she gains a point of Initiative.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00B30F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Unseen Forest Spirit </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: \u2014; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Permanent</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Permanent</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Invisible Statue Spirit, Leaf-Whisper Imitation</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">This Evocation upgrades Invisible Statue Spirit (Exalted, p. 403). While the Solar is in plant-based concealment, the Charm\u2019s cost is waived.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01B81E\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Trackless Jungle</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: \u2014; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Permanent</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Permanent</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Elusive Forest Shadow, Traceless Passage</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">This Evocation upgrades Traceless Passage (Exalted, p. 412). When the Solar uses it to conceal her tracks while moving through a forest, jungle, or other vegetation-dense terrain, she doubles 7s.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1DB100\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Lightness of the Birch-Tree</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Simple</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Armoured Scout\u2019s Invigoration, Leaf-Whisper Imitation</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When activated, this Evocation removes Ebony Fronds\u2019 mobility penalty.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1DB100\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Toughness of the Cedar</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Simple</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Lightness of the Birch-Tree</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Given a moment\u2019s preparation, the wearer of the armour can cause its scales to grow a bark-like layer of additional protection, increasing Ebony Fronds\u2019 Soak by 2.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1DB100\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Ghost Who Walks</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 5m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 5</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Reflexive</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Resonant</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Trackless Jungle, Toughness of the Cedar</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When the character reaches Incapacitated, this Charm both stabilizes the wearer and creates the illusion that the wearer is indeed dead. The illusion remains for as long as the armour is attuned and the Evocation\u2019s motes committed, and can be penetrated with a Difficulty 5 Perception+Awareness roll.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no cost the first time the wearer is reduced to Incapacitated.</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T22:47:36-07:00","id":1400904,"title":"","content":"Leaf-Whisper Imitation: 2m<br /> <br /> Trackless Jungle: Doubling 7s is a bit overkill. You might as well not exist as I don't think anyone could oppose that realistically. Make it a reroll to cover tracks instead, charms reactivated for free on second roll, and you keep the better of two results. This makes it a bit easier to recover from a bad roll but is not an autowin charm.<br /> <br /> Lightness of the Birch-Tree: Boring and pretty much pointless. Is 2m really worth the one point of mobility penalty? In most cases, no.<br /> <br /> Toughness of the Cedar: Boring. I'd give some side benefit, like letting the wielder subsist off sunlight in addition to the soak.<br /> <br /> Ghost Who Walks: This is Essence 3 at most. Stablization isn't that big of a deal. If you want to make it spicy, make it Essence 4, Duration instant, and the ability to let the Exalt live after a blow that would've plainly killed him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 07-04-2020, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:32:48-07:00","id":1400975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1400904#post1400904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaf-Whisper Imitation: 2m<br /> <br /> Trackless Jungle: Doubling 7s is a bit overkill. You might as well not exist as I don't think anyone could oppose that realistically. Make it a reroll to cover tracks instead, charms reactivated for free on second roll, and you keep the better of two results. This makes it a bit easier to recover from a bad roll but is not an autowin charm.<br /> <br /> Lightness of the Birch-Tree: Boring and pretty much pointless. Is 2m really worth the one point of mobility penalty? In most cases, no.<br /> <br /> Toughness of the Cedar: Boring. I'd give some side benefit, like letting the wielder subsist off sunlight in addition to the soak.<br /> <br /> Ghost Who Walks: This is Essence 3 at most. Stablization isn't that big of a deal. If you want to make it spicy, make it Essence 4, Duration instant, and the ability to let the Exalt live after a blow that would've plainly killed him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double 8s, or perhaps 9s for Trackless Jungle.<br /> <br /> Lightness of the Birch-Tree is a less expensive version of Armoured Scout's Invigoration.<br /> <br /> &quot;Boring&quot; and &quot;simple&quot; are not the same. I consider Toughness of the Cedar to be the latter.<br /> <br /> Ghost Who Walks: I fail to see the difference between automatic stabilization at Incapacitated and &quot;let the Exalt live after a blow that would've plainly killed him.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T12:25:04-07:00","id":1400986,"title":"","content":"Double 9s would work, but you need to remember that doublers can get out of hand very quickly. I don't know what artifact level this is, but by guessing on the effects I'd say a 3. Double 7s is way too strong, but a double 9 or a reroller is easily within that power.<br /> <br /> Armoured Scout's Invigoration is terrible. It's overly expensive and those delving into armour really won't care about it's penalties. The only real point of significance is the -1 evasion. If you want it to be better, make it a 0m permanent effect. Reduce the mobility penalty of the armour to 0 and reduce any penalties related to mobility/Stealth through dense underbrush by 2 (Or 1 from defenses). This makes it more useful and stands out in a niche way that suits using it for it's designed environment.<br /> <br /> Simple charms are often basic effects early on or effects that while fairly straightforward are extremely powerful. This doesn't apply here. Boring in this case is when you know you can do better, especially for an Essence 3 charm, where effects generally leave the simple territory. Subsisting off sunlight is a basic niche but welcome effect. You can substitute anything else you want, I was trying to give it more spice. Make a charm that's &quot;Wow that's really cool, I'm going to take that&quot; vs &quot;More soak is always nice I guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hitting incap in 3e doesn't mean you automatically die. What I would be proposing is a counter to effects that go &quot;Kill this person upon death&quot;. Such as Soul Mastery, that one Solar charm in Miracles, or ST fiat by saying getting hit with a mountain destroying vaporizer cannon would also vaporize your character. Again, a bit niche. Such a power won't stop a dedicated foe from crub stomping you when you're down, but it would help in a major fight where you allies could drag you off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T14:21:13-07:00","id":1401000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1400986#post1400986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hitting incap in 3e doesn't mean you automatically die. What I would be proposing is a counter to effects that go &quot;Kill this person upon death&quot;. Such as Soul Mastery, that one Solar charm in Miracles, or ST fiat by saying getting hit with a mountain destroying vaporizer cannon would also vaporize your character. Again, a bit niche. Such a power won't stop a dedicated foe from crub stomping you when you're down, but it would help in a major fight where you allies could drag you off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the illusion effect that convinces onlookers that the wearer is indeed dead. Though I haven't yet read through Dragon Blooded, so didn't know that Soul Mastery was still around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T14:55:01-07:00","id":1401005,"title":"","content":"I'm not a big fan of &quot;play dead&quot; mechanics, because it develops a mentality that leads to players double-tapping and otherwise gruesomely mutilating the foes they defeat, and that's just not the kind of game I enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T20:45:39-07:00","id":1401045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401005#post1401005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a big fan of &quot;play dead&quot; mechanics, because it develops a mentality that leads to players double-tapping and otherwise gruesomely mutilating the foes they defeat, and that's just not the kind of game I enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has this really happened to you? I've never had this happen in my games. The only times I've seen it happen is when an opponent falls for it once then makes sure to cut off the head next time to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T21:51:52-07:00","id":1401049,"title":"","content":"Main thing I've experienced when this trick gets pulled is annoyed Zenith players who insist they've done enough on-screen to show they've taken care of the recently deceased (including burning bodies) that this trick working requires them to be out of character.<br /> <br /> There was also a whole thing with the Ebon Shadow Style charm Image of Death Technique.<br /> <br /> Basically, a fellow player recognised an NPC was using Ebon Shadow Style and thus knew in advance that the character had access to a charm to fake their death leading to an argument about using knowledge from the books. It highlighted IoDT was a bad charm since Ebon Shadow Form doesn't normally leave a body behind thus the style kinda outed its own trick. It was replaced by Nothing But Shadows which has a different primary function and the way the fake your death option works is built on a combat action which leaves it less open for &quot;why didn't we burn the body?&quot; style conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 07-05-2020, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T22:09:58-07:00","id":1401052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401045#post1401045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this really happened to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Over and over.<br /> <br /> Also, this shit happens in real life; there\u2019s a reason playing possum is outlawed under the Geneva Conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-05-2020, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T11:08:32-07:00","id":1401152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401045#post1401045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Has this really happened to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never had an enemy fake death, and my PCs still mutilate corpses &quot;just in case they're a Lunar&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T11:52:10-07:00","id":1401157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401152#post1401152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had an enemy fake death, and my PCs still mutilate corpses &quot;just in case they're a Lunar&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine do the same &quot;because what if they're an Abyssal&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T12:23:34-07:00","id":1401163,"title":"","content":"Wow OK. I've never literally ever had this happen in a game, barring an NPC had a fake death ability then used that to elude the players once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T12:33:50-07:00","id":1401168,"title":"","content":"My players do it all the time depending on context. They won't randomly mincemeat and burn any mortal they come across, but if they're suspicious that there might be more going on, like spirit blooded or an exalt they totally will. It might be a bit of a holdover from DnD where anything less than true ressurection requires a body, so if you want death to stick harder don't leave a body. I once had a group fully roll over a kraken's health pool at least once, risking their own lives due to lack of air at the bottom of the ocean, doing that.<br /> <br /> In Exalted though, burning the body and taking care of funerary rights and stuff prevents underworld shit, even without the possibility that they might be playing dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T13:19:42-07:00","id":1401179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401163#post1401163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow OK. I've never literally ever had this happen in a game, barring an NPC had a fake death ability then used that to elude the players once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what the good Doc said. Mine won't do it to mortals, but obviously supernatural sentient beings get a beheading. Which really sucks if you're a Liminal since being hard to kill is supposed to be your thing, but then along comes the Paranoia Circle and BOOM, no more Liminal without them even knowing what they faced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T14:22:25-07:00","id":1401189,"title":"","content":"I feel like the answer to this is to use the settings 'respect the dead or the dead cause Problems' rules??? Like I feel like &quot;You mutilated my body' should be a good way to justify some serious murderghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T16:16:51-07:00","id":1401214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401189#post1401189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the answer to this is to use the settings 'respect the dead or the dead cause Problems' rules??? Like I feel like &quot;You mutilated my body' should be a good way to justify some serious murderghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, a hungry ghost with a destroyed body lacks a place to hide from the sunlight that destroys it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, Zenith Castes can prevent a hungry ghost from rising.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T16:29:12-07:00","id":1401217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401214#post1401214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlso, Zenith Castes can prevent a hungry ghost from rising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which incidentally also incinerates the corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T16:39:54-07:00","id":1401219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401214#post1401214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, a hungry ghost with a destroyed body lacks a place to hide from the sunlight that destroys it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, Zenith Castes can prevent a hungry ghost from rising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well part of what I mean is put in some consequences for being corpse mutilating psychopaths. The setting has room for it, and really corpse mutilating should be saved for people you *realllly* hate. Zeniths can make sure that particular body/person doesn't ghostify, but what about their loved ones? Or what about their ancestors, who may become aware that a horrible crime has beend committed upon the body of one of their descendants.<br /> Most people do *Not* take well to others fucking around with bodies, in any way. Even just battlefield looting, a crime of relative unimportance and significant practicality is often seen as, at best, goulish. So I can't imagine gods and spirits and such would be particularly approving.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh and I just thought of, honestly Zeniths shouldn't *NEED* to mutilate *any* corpses anyway so it shouldn't be a problem. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23941,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","user":"Aquatica","date":". 07-05-2020, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T17:06:54-07:00","id":1401223,"title":"","content":"My point is, these &quot;play dead&quot; powers never seem to account for what happens once genre-savvy player characters decide to do something <i>other than</i> just leaving the character feigning their death (henceforth referred to as &quot;the possum&quot;) and going about their business.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf they give the possum a proper burial or cremation, he dies.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf they use the Zenith Caste anima power to cremate the possum, he's revealed as not actually being dead, and then they kill him.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf they don't have a Zenith and decide to &quot;make sure&quot; the possum is dead, he dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T17:19:47-07:00","id":1401227,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel like fake death is more interesting in the hands of players than antagonists for pretty much those reasons. Or as temporary 'you turned your back on what you thought was a corpse, and then they get back up and try and shank you in the back.' It doesn't work so well against players as a long con.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T18:13:04-07:00","id":1401240,"title":"","content":"If it matters, the armour is intended for a PC, and my STs don't believe in having NPCs &quot;kill them again&quot; just on general principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T18:47:05-07:00","id":1401244,"title":"","content":"Then that sounds fine to me! My apologies, I got distracted by morbid discussion!<br /> For that Evocation tho, I'd honestly suggest making it actually heal. Put it at like, essence 4 instead of 5, and let them roll a small amount of healing in addition to not dying. I'd raise the cost a bit to match, but that'd make it more useful for situations beyond 'fake death.' Could be a nice second wind trick. Essence five just for 'not dying on Incapacitated and fake death' is a bit higher than I think it should be, even for 5 motes.<br /> Though it does matter, what artifact rating is this? (If I just somehow missed that, oops!)<br /> Thematically, I think you should add some 'useful fluff' to the very simple evocations. Stuff that's *maybe* useful for something small. Growth and nature as a theme mean's maybe using<br /> <br /> Now if you wanted my suggestion for an essence 5 fake death Evocation, something like as you &quot;die&quot;, your body is pulled into the earth and an double is created. The double is enough like you, carrying your wounds, etc. This happens shrouded in illusion so that it looks like you're just *dying.* You remain beneath the earth, healing somewhat faster (but not 'leap right back into the same combat' faster. Maybe fast enough that if they decide to for some godawful reason camp out near you you can get the jump on them.) Mastery effect of something that lets you move undetected away, so that when you show up later you really do seem to be a fucking ghost. Now that'd be spooky, to me, though probably less to the inhabitants of Creation, considering that the undead are a fairly common concern.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T00:23:16-07:00","id":1401290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400898-armour-evocations-feedback-requested?p=1401189#post1401189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the answer to this is to use the settings 'respect the dead or the dead cause Problems' rules??? Like I feel like &quot;You mutilated my body' should be a good way to justify some serious murderghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to beat a dead horse(ha!), but I just woke up and wanted clarify that yeah it does cause problems. Depending on the group's charateristics they just sometimes feel it's worth it. When I have a Xenith or DB with Soul-Fire Cremation Technique this doesn't happen. Or when someone is playing a really righteous type it also doesn't happen, and when it does they're often discrete about it. I realized my group my get mad if they read that I was making them sound like psychos(even if they are :P) without some clarification.<br /> <br /> Moving on, I like your suggestion Aquatica and I agree the level of the artifact really matters here. A 5 dot artifact for instance, is likely to have effect far reaching beyond supplementing simple abilities. The play dead effect could also be given an extra psyche effect vs their resolve that has to be gotten past to even roll for seeing through the illusion. Or perhaps it allows for a certain amount of spill over to simply be stopped at incapacitated and overrules the ST on what happens to the characters fate at that point. I mean at incapacitated your kinda at the ST's mercy but if you're going to take 7 dmg over that they're more likely to rule you dead. This is an essence 5 evocation capstone after all, regardless of the artifacts rating deciding how it should be expressed it still needs some serious oomph to justify it's existence. Though getting it for free is pretty cool, it doesn't matter one whit if the character actually ends up dying( which if their incapacitated lvl is marked through with lethal damage they very well could be per pg 173 Ex3 Core).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T02:49:59-07:00","id":1401309,"title":"","content":"The armour is Artifact 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T06:56:05-07:00","id":1401674,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The revised version.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ebony Fronds (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022 Lamellar Armour)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Forged during the Shogunate, Ebony Fronds was first forged from steel and green jade, heated over ancient willow charcoal, then tempered with vegetable oil and soap and the sap of certain Eastern thistles for the Eastern Outcaste Busujima Clan\u2019s eldest son, Shutaro, who wore it in many battles and in time of peace, set it where rain and sun could reach it. In due course, it passed into the hands of other sons, and less often daughters, of the Clan. As with their other great treasures, the Clan took great pride in knowing that they had never had to ransom it back from their enemies. After the clan\u2019s destruction, it passed into the hands of Saeko Takagi, their former retainer and recently Exalted Dawn Caste.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Created for a man noted for his fastidious nature, the armour keeps itself and its attuned wearer clean, as per the Collar of Dawn\u2019s Cleansing Light. Given the great difficulty of keeping lamellar armour clean and pest-free with its intricate lacings, this is a considerable benefit. It also incorporates a hearthstone socket, which currently holds the keep\u2019s Monkey Stone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Evocations of Ebony Fronds</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Leaf-Whisper Imitation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Resonant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Ebony Fronds\u2019 overlapping scales become as silent and soft as leaves. This Evocation enhances a Stealth roll made while in plant-based concealment, lowering any penalties by the wearer\u2019s (Essence).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Special activation rules</b>: As long as the wearer isn\u2019t dissonant with jade, this Evocation awakens at no cost when she successfully ambushes a non-trivial enemy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Resonant</b>: As long as the wearer\u2019s roll beats at least one non-trivial enemy, she gains a point of Initiative.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00B30F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Unseen Forest Spirit </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: \u2014; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Invisible Statue Spirit, Leaf-Whisper Imitation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">This Evocation upgrades Invisible Statue Spirit (Exalted, p. 403). While the Solar is in plant-based concealment, the Charm\u2019s cost is waived.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01B81E\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Trackless Jungle</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: \u2014; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Elusive Forest Shadow, Traceless Passage</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">This Evocation upgrades Traceless Passage (Exalted, p. 412). When the Solar uses it to conceal her tracks while moving through a forest, jungle, or other vegetation-dense terrain, she doubles 8s.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1DB100\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Lightness of the Birch-Tree</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Armoured Scout\u2019s Invigoration, Leaf-Whisper Imitation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When activated, this Evocation removes Ebony Fronds\u2019 mobility penalty.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1DB100\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Toughness of the Cedar</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Lightness of the Birch-Tree</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Given a moment\u2019s preparation, the wearer of the armour can cause its scales to grow a bark-like layer of additional protection, increasing Ebony Fronds\u2019 Soak by 2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1DB100\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Ghost Who Walks</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 5m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Resonant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Trackless Jungle, Toughness of the Cedar</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When the wearer suffers an attack that would normally kill her, the armour instead buries her and itself, leaving an illusionary copy behind. The illusion remains for as long as the armour is attuned and the Evocation\u2019s motes committed, and can be penetrated with a Difficulty 5 Perception+Awareness roll. The wearer is stabilized automatically, and the armour provides life support and speeds healing by a factor of 2 while the armour remains attuned and the Evocation\u2019s motes remain committed. At the Charm\u2019s end, the illusion ends and the armour automatically unburies itself and its wearer.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no cost the first time the wearer is reduced to Incapacitated.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}